---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy – Transparent Data & Cookies Notice"
  description={`How ${siteConfig.name} handles preferences, local storage, advertising cookies, and browser permissions.`}
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <article class="content-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Plain-Language Policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p>
      Last updated: September 2026. At {siteConfig.name}, we believe in transparent, minimalist data
      practices. We do not require user accounts, passwords, or personal profiles. All core
      device-clock, stopwatch, timer, alarm and time-zone calculations run within your web browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Local Storage and Preferences</h2>
    <p>
      Your user preferences—including saved timer presets, active alarm schedules, preferred world
      clock cities, time zone converter pairings, and light/dark theme selection—are stored
      exclusively in your browser's
      <code>localStorage</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Running countdown timers store an end-timestamp in <code>sessionStorage</code> so that refreshing
      the tab restores the countdown when session storage is available. Closing the tab can clear this
      state. None of this data is ever transmitted to or stored on our servers.
    </p>

    <h2>Ticket website time checks</h2>
    <p>
      When you request a ticket time check, our hosting service receives the selected website ID and
      queries that website's public response timestamp. The upstream request does not forward your
      cookies, IP address, login details or countdown input. Measured time samples may be shared in
      a hosting cache for up to ten seconds; they contain the website ID and timing data, not
      visitor records. Countdown input remains in this page's memory. Standard hosting logs may
      include your request path and IP address as described below.
    </p>
    <h2>Advertising review and cookies</h2><p>
      As of September 30, 2026, advertising is disabled. Account metadata and ads.txt identify the
      site for AdSense review without loading the advertising script. The following information
      applies if advertising is enabled in a future release.
    </p>
    <p>
      To help support the ongoing hosting and development of our free instruments, {siteConfig.name} may
      use third-party advertising partners, including <strong>Google AdSense</strong>.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior
        visits to this website or other websites on the Internet.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve personalized or
        non-personalized ads based on your visits to our site and other sites across the web.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your Choices & Opt-Out:</strong> You may opt out of personalized advertising at any time
        by visiting
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Google Ads Settings</a
        >. Alternatively, you can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized
        advertising by visiting
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >www.aboutads.info</a
        >.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Server Logs & Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      When you load pages on {siteConfig.name}, our static hosting provider automatically receives
      standard HTTP request metadata, such as your IP address, browser user-agent, and the requested
      page URL. This technical data is used solely for content delivery, DDOS mitigation, and server
      security.
    </p>

    <h2>Browser Permissions (Notifications & Wake Lock)</h2>
    <p>
      We will only request browser permissions when you explicitly click a corresponding control:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Notifications:</strong> Used solely to alert you when an alarm or timer completes. You
        can revoke notification privileges at any time in your browser settings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Screen Wake Lock:</strong> Used solely when you enable the "Keep screen awake" toggle
        on the clock or timer, preventing your display from dimming during study or cooking sessions.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to Delete Your Data</h2>
    <p>
      Because your data is saved only in your device's browser, you have complete control. You can
      delete individual alarms or saved cities directly inside the app, or clear your browser's
      cookies and site data for
      <code>{siteConfig.name}</code> to permanently wipe all stored settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Email inquiries</h2><p>
      If you email us, your address and message are received in the operator’s Gmail mailbox and
      used to respond. Do not include passwords or sensitive records. Contact us to request deletion
      of correspondence.
    </p><h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about our privacy practices, please contact us at
      <a href="mailto:jacho0227@gmail.com">jacho0227@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
